          {
            "id": "element-14",
            "type": "text",
            "x": 477.87,
            "y": 138.16,
            "w": 754.76,
            "h": 110.94,
            "fill": "transparent",
            "stroke": "transparent",
            "strokeWidth": 0,
            "text": "LTC Ally’s SDLC and QA controls sufficient but immature; formalized testing and standardized delivery processes can improve stability and velocity\nThe platform has foundational SDLC controls in place, but variation in team execution and limited engineering KPIs reduce visibility into delivery consistency and product iteration speed; standardized team practices can ensure product quality and consistency\nPlatform testing is embedded in the release process through API testing, functional QA, and UAT, but limited code coverage tracking,  and limited load testing reduce confidence in release quality at scale; A formalized testing standard can improve platform stability",
            "align": "left",
            "valign": "top",
            "fontSize": 11,
            "fontFace": "Arial",
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "111827",
            "runs": [
              {
                "text": "LTC Ally’s SDLC and QA controls sufficient but immature; formalized testing and standardized delivery processes can improve stability and velocity",
                "bold": true,
                "color": "111827",
                "fontFace": "Arial",
                "fontSize": 11,
                "breakLine": true
              },
              {
                "text": "The platform has foundational SDLC controls in place, but variation in team execution and limited engineering KPIs reduce visibility into delivery consistency and product iteration speed; standardized team practices can ensure product quality and consistency",
                "color": "111827",
                "fontFace": "Arial",
                "fontSize": 9,
                "breakLine": true
              },
              {
                "text": "Platform testing is embedded in the release process through API testing, functional QA, and UAT, but limited code coverage tracking,  and limited load testing reduce confidence in release quality at scale; A formalized testing standard can improve platform stability",
                "color": "111827",
                "fontFace": "Arial",
                "fontSize": 9,
                "breakLine": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "element-15",
            "type": "text",
            "x": 471.51,
            "y": 267.94,
            "w": 754.76,
            "h": 125.48,
            "fill": "transparent",
            "stroke": "transparent",
            "strokeWidth": 0,
            "text": "Manual operational reliance of the platform limits growth potential; automation of workflows introduces speed ang agility, positioning the company well for expansion\nCore ECS workloads appear to be manually scaled, and Aging Tracking still includes a manual deployment step, increasing operational effort and limiting elastic scalability. Implementing auto-scaling can enhance efficiency, increase flexibility, and improve scale readiness\nDeployment processes appear partially manual, increasing operational effort and person-dependency while slowing releases. Greater deployment automation can improve efficiency, consistency, and release readiness",
            "align": "left",
            "valign": "top",
            "fontSize": 11,
            "fontFace": "ヒラギノ角ゴ Pro W3",
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "111827",
            "runs": [
              {
                "text": "Manual operational reliance of the platform limits growth potential; automation of workflows introduces speed ang agility, positioning the company well for expansion",
                "bold": true,
                "color": "111827",
                "fontFace": "ヒラギノ角ゴ Pro W3",
                "fontSize": 11,
                "breakLine": true
              },
              {
                "text": "Core ECS workloads appear to be manually scaled, and Aging Tracking still includes a manual deployment step, increasing operational effort and limiting elastic scalability. Implementing auto-scaling can enhance efficiency, increase flexibility, and improve scale readiness",
                "color": "111827",
                "fontFace": "Arial",
                "fontSize": 9,
                "breakLine": true
              },
              {
                "text": "Deployment processes appear partially manual, increasing operational effort and person-dependency while slowing releases. Greater deployment automation can improve efficiency, consistency, and release readiness",
                "color": "111827",
                "fontFace": "Arial",
                "fontSize": 9,
                "breakLine": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "element-16",
            "type": "text",
            "x": 472.76,
            "y": 391.28,
            "w": 754.76,
            "h": 96.4,
            "fill": "transparent",
            "stroke": "transparent",
            "strokeWidth": 0,
            "text": "Platform has limited application monitoring and alerting; broader monitoring coverage and increased alerting across critical applications can increase resolution speed\nEngineering KPIs and portfolio-wide health metrics appear limited beyond ticket-level tracking and baseline monitoring, reducing visibility into platform health which can lead to long term failures; Platform-wide metrics can lead to proactive resolutions\nAlerting coverage appears uneven across critical applications and integrations, limiting proactive visibility into recurring issues and increasing reliance on manual escalation; appropriate monitoring can lead to faster error resolutions",
            "align": "left",
            "valign": "top",
            "fontSize": 11,
            "fontFace": "Arial",
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "111827",
            "runs": [
              {
                "text": "Platform has limited application monitoring and alerting; broader monitoring coverage and increased alerting across critical applications can increase resolution speed",
                "bold": true,
                "color": "111827",
                "fontFace": "Arial",
                "fontSize": 11,
                "breakLine": true
              },
              {
                "text": "Engineering KPIs and portfolio-wide health metrics appear limited beyond ticket-level tracking and baseline monitoring, reducing visibility into platform health which can lead to long term failures; Platform-wide metrics can lead to proactive resolutions",
                "color": "111827",
                "fontFace": "Arial",
                "fontSize": 9,
                "breakLine": true
              },
              {
                "text": "Alerting coverage appears uneven across critical applications and integrations, limiting proactive visibility into recurring issues and increasing reliance on manual escalation; appropriate monitoring can lead to faster error resolutions",
                "color": "111827",
                "fontFace": "Arial",
                "fontSize": 9,
                "breakLine": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "element-19",
            "type": "text",
            "x": 474.9,
            "y": 510.32,
            "w": 754.76,
            "h": 110.94,
            "fill": "transparent",
            "stroke": "transparent",
            "strokeWidth": 0,
            "text": "Although GenAI is said to be gaining traction, qualitative monitoring limits management’s ability to measure productivity, quality, and cost impact\nAdoption appears to be tracked primarily through developer self-reporting and ticket annotations, with management following up through verbal check-ins rather than through automated usage or code-generation metrics, limiting reliability given potential inconsistency, underreporting, or subjective inputs\nWhile management cited examples of faster task execution and qualitative productivity gains, the company does not appear to have a consistent pre/post-AI measurement framework reducing visibility into ROI and cost control",
            "align": "left",
            "valign": "top",
            "fontSize": 11,
            "fontFace": "Arial",
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "111827",
            "runs": [
              {
                "text": "Although GenAI is said to be gaining traction, qualitative monitoring limits management’s ability to measure productivity, quality, and cost impact",
                "bold": true,
